                <pb facs="0965" n="839" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg839"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A 4 e/263: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-08-10T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 10,
                                1925—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>198. Your 320, August 8, 10 a.m. I approve views set forth in paragraphs 2 and 3
                    of your telegram. If an identic note along lines of American draft communicated
                    in my telegram No. 165 July 23, 3 p.m.<anchor n="52" xml:id="d689-f1"/> is
                    adopted this should satisfy Chinese as regards scope of conference and serve as
                    preliminary basis of conference agenda. Otherwise it would be better to go into
                    the conference on the basis of the treaty and leave conference to develop and to
                    obtain authority to deal with such further matters as its deliberations might
                    prove necessary or advisable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
